# LLM answering configuration for the dashboard comparison experiments.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit the real .env (already gitignored).
# The backend reads these ON DEMAND at call time; nothing is hardcoded.

# Generic names (preferred):
LLM_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
LLM_BASE_URL=https://your-api-base/v1
LLM_MODEL=your-model-id
#
# IMPORTANT — pin a CONCRETE, general-purpose model id. A routing alias such
# as OpenRouter's "openrouter/free" picks a DIFFERENT backend on every call.
# Observed live: it can land on a content-safety model that returns the literal
# string "User Safety: safe" instead of an answer, or a reasoning model that
# spends the whole token budget on chain-of-thought (empty answer). This
# backend now detects those non-answering replies and raises a clear error,
# but only a pinned general assistant (e.g. "meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct")
# guarantees a real natural-language answer. Do NOT set LLM_MODEL to an alias.

# Legacy OpenAI-style names are also accepted as fallbacks:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=...
# OPENAI_MODEL=...
